⚠️ Ek Important Kaam — .env Ko Git Se Hata
Tune pehle .env file commit kar di thi. Ab usko GitHub se hata de (kyunki usme API keys daalni hain, public nahi honi chahiye):

powershell
git rm --cached backend/.env
git rm --cached frontend/.env
git commit -m "Remove .env files from tracking"
git push
Ye command .env file ko locally rakhegi, lekin GitHub se hata degi.

🎯 Uske Baad
Ab tujhe 2 aur files chahiye:

backend/.env.example — sample env (without real keys)

frontend/.env.example — sample env

Bolo, wo bhi de doon? Ya ab backend ka actual code start karun? 🚀

Bata bhai:

"env example de" → dono .env.example files dunga

"backend code de" → main.py se start karke pura backend file-by-file dunga

"frontend code de" → React ka pura code dunga

Bas bata. 💪



